Z||000000||mrfiero||09-12-2000||06:04 PM||||Does anyone here have an ADS superchip?  I just picked one up from an '86 SE (V-6, 4-sp.) and need to find out if it went to that car or ??  The ECM was lying on the floor and the chip coverplate was off.  I pulled out the chip and now just need to find out what I have.<P>On the top is a red sticker that says "ADS Superchip".  Molded into the plastic carrier is "RN" and "1" with a circle around it.  On the bottom (by the pins) is a code.....40420910BN.  Below that it says "PHILLIPINES LX 04".<P>Any help would be appreciated.<P><BR>    ||||reg||5
Z||000001||wkayl||09-12-2000||07:26 PM||||Was the ECM the only one in the car or was this an extra one?  (My 86GT has an automatic)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||09-12-2000||07:33 PM||||It was the only one in the car.  I'm pretty sure it came from that particular Fiero, but you never know if it's the correct chip (might be another one?).<P>The engine and tranny (whole cradle) was gone by the time I found this one, so they must've pulled the ECM to disconnect the wiring.  <P>Will a chip from a manual Fiero work on an auto.?<P>If you're interested you can drive down and we'll install it to find out.  You can pick  up that deflector too.<P>LMK.<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-12-2000||09:06 PM||||There should be a label on the bottom (white) like "8604A" or "8604CA".<P>No, a manual chip won't work in an automatic. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||09-13-2000||01:04 AM||||No label.....it look slike there is some glue residue where those numbers are....the sticker likely fell off.<P>I didn't think the chips were interchangeable....it didn't make sense, but you never know.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
